{"id":"word:hebrew:H5127","type":"word","title":"נוּס","subtitle":"H5127 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to flit , i.e. vanish away (subside, escape; causatively, chase, impel, deliver)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נוּס (H5127) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 161 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נוּס (nûwç) means to flit , i.e. vanish away (subside, escape; causatively, chase, impel, deliver) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 10 1."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נוּס","transliteration":"nûwç","pronunciation":"noos","strong":"H5127","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5127","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יָּנֻ֖סוּ","נָ֖סוּ","נָ֣ס","וַ/יָּ֣נָס","לָ/נ֖וּס"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqw3mp",31],["HC/Vqw3ms",22],["HVqp3ms",13],["HR/Vqc",13],["HVqp3cp",11],["HVqi3ms",8],["HC/Vqq3ms",7],["HVqrmpa",5],["HC/Vqq3cp",4],["HVqv2mp",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"to flit , i.e. vanish away (subside, escape; causatively, chase, impel, deliver)","usage":"× abate, away, be displayed, (make to) flee (away, -ing), put to flight, × hide, lift up a standard.","full":"H5127. nus נוּס 160 verb flee, escape (Syriac tremble (rare), compare Brock; Arabic move to and fro, be in commotion, dangle , Lane 2866 ); — Qal Perfect נָס Num 35:25 +; נַ֫סְתָּה 2Kin 9:3 ; נַ֫סְתִּי 1Sam 4:16 , etc.; Imperfect יָנוּס Exod 21:13 +; וַיָּנָ֫ס Gen 39:12 +; יְנוּס֑וּן Psa 104:7 , etc.; Imperative masculine plural נֻ֫סוּ Jer 48:6 4 t. Jeremiah, Zechariah; Infinitive absolute נוֺס 2Sam 18:3 ; construct לָנוּס ( לָנֻס ) Gen 19:20 +; Participle נָס Amos 9:1 +; נָסִים Exod 14:27 +; — 1 flee , absolute Gen 39:12 , 15 ; Num 16:34 (all J); Josh 10:16 (JE); Lev 26:17 , 36 ; (H); figurative of sea Psa 114:3 ; 114:5 ; compare 104:7 ; followed by accusative of congnate meaning with verb מָנוֺס Jer 46:5 , followed by דֶּרֶךְ Josh 8:15 (J), 2Kin 9:27 ; followed by בְּדֶרֶךְ Deut 28:7 , 25 ; ׳נ אֶלנַֿפְשָׁם 2Kin 7:7 flee for their life , ׳נ בְּרַגְלָיו , Judg 4:15 flee on foot ; + 44 t. absolute (not elsewhere Hexateuch); followed by אֶלֿ location Deut 4:42 ; 19:5 , 11 (D), Num 35:32 ; Josh 20:4 (both P), Judg 4:17 ; 1Kin 2:28-29 , Isa 13:14 ; followed by לְ 1Sam 4:10 6 t. + לִקְרָאתוֺ Exod 14:27 (E; not elsewhere Hexateuch); followed by עַד Judg 7:22 + Prov 28:17 ( עַדבּֿוֺר , see בּוֺר ); followed by עַלֿ Isa 10:3 ; followed by ָ ה locative Gen 14:10 4 t. J E, Num 35:6 6 t. P, Deut 4:42 ; 19:3-4 , (D), + 6 t.; followed by שָׁם Isa 20:6 ; followed by accusative of location Josh 8:20 (J), + 4 t.; followed by מִמֶּרְחָק Isa 17:13 = far away ; followed by מִן from, Josh 20:6 (P), 1Sam 4:16 3 t.; מִתּוֺךְ Jer 51:6 ; especially מִמְּנֵי from before Exod 4:3 ; 14:25 ; Num 10:35 ; Josh 10:11 (all J E), 1Sam 17:24 ; Jer 48:44 (Qr הַנָּס , &gt; Kt הניס ), + 19 t.; followed by לִפְנֵי Josh 7:4 ; 8:5 (twice in verse); 8:6 (all J), 1Sam 4:17 ; 2Sam 24:13 , מִלִּפְנֵי 1Chr 19:18 . 2 escape Amos 9:1 (|| נמלט ) so Jer 46:6 ; hence 3 take flight, depart, disappear , only figurative; Deut 34:7 (JE) his freshness ( לֵחֹה vigour ) was not gone (|| עינו כָֽהֲתָה לֹא ); of shadows (at evening), Song 2:17 ; 4:6 ; of sorrow etc. Isa 35:10 ; 51:11 . 4 ׳נ עַלסֿוּס Isa 30:16 fly (to the attack) on horseback . Po`lel Perfect Isa 59:19 י ׳רוּחַ בּוֺ נֹסֲסָה the breath of ׳י driveth at it, driveth it on (compare Hiph`il 2 ). Hithpo`l. Infinitive construct מִמְּנֵי לְהִתְנוֺסֵס Psa 60:6 in order to take flight before the bow (so Vrss Hup-Now Che Bae and others). Hiph`il Perfect הֵנִיס Exod 9:20 ; Imperfect יָנִיסוּ Deut 32:30 + Judg 7:21 Kt (Qr וַיָּנוּסוּ Qal ); Infinitive construct לְתָנִיס Judg 6:11 ; &#8212; 1 put to flight , followed by accusative Deut 32:30 (|| רדף ). 2 drive hastily to a safe place Exod 9:20 , followed by accusative + אֶלֿ . 3 cause to disappear, hide Judg 6:11 (no object expressed) followed by מִמְּנֵי .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["